    {
      "id": "02-create",
      "instruction": "In the Odoo Sales app, create a new quotation (Sales > Orders > Quotations > New). Set the Customer field to '{{runid}} Bench Customer' by typing the name and picking the matching option from the autocomplete dropdown (the value only counts if chosen from the dropdown). Then add exactly ONE order line: in the order lines table, pick any product from the product catalogue by typing in the product autocomplete and choosing an option from the dropdown, and set its Quantity to 3. Let the app fill in the unit price automatically. Do NOT add any other line. Save the quotation. Then report: (a) the exact product name you chose, (b) the unit price the app filled in for that line, and (c) the Untaxed Amount shown in the totals section of the quotation.",
      "outputs": [
        "customer_name",
        "customer_city_shown",
        "product_name",
        "quantity",
        "unit_price",
        "untaxed_amount",
        "tax_20",
        "total",
        "order_line_count",
        "quotation_number",
        "blocking_modal"
      ],
      "recorded": {
        "customer_name": "fwod69-n1 Bench Customer",
        "customer_city_shown": "Benchville",
